course: dictionary
lesson: 15783
title: Ugliness: looks and actions
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Ugliness is a noun. It names the quality of being ugly, which means very unpleasant to look at. Its opposite is beauty.
explain: «The rubbish heap had a sad ugliness that made Sam look away.» Sam did not like how the heap looked, so here ugliness means the unpleasant look of something.
explain: Ugliness can also mean nastiness in how people behave. «The ugliness of bullying hurts everyone who sees it.» Here the word is about cruel actions, not faces. Ugliness is uncountable, so we say «the ugliness», not «an ugliness».
fact: Ugliness is a noun: it names a quality.
fact: «Ugliness» means being very unpleasant to look at.
fact: «Ugliness» can also mean cruelty or nastiness in how people act.
fact: In The Ugly Duckling, the duckling is teased for its looks, but it grows into a beautiful swan.
fact: Ugliness is uncountable, so we say «the ugliness», not «an ugliness».
exercise: In «The rubbish heap had a sad ugliness that made Sam look away.», what does ugliness mean? | Being very tall | *Being very unpleasant to look at | Being very loud and noisy | Being very kind to animals
exercise: «The ugliness of bullying hurts everyone who sees it.» Does ugliness here mean looks or behaviour? | Looks | Size | Colour | *Behaviour, meaning nastiness or cruelty
exercise: Which word is the opposite of ugliness? | Darkness | Noise | *Beauty | Sadness
test: Is ugliness a noun or a verb? | *Noun | Adverb | Adjective | Verb
test: In The Ugly Duckling, what does the duckling become? | *A beautiful swan | A frog | A bee | A dog
exam: Which sentence uses ugliness correctly? | I ugliness the ball across the park. | Ugliness is a very happy dog. | *The ugliness of war made the whole town sad. | The ugliness ran very fast home.
